    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "i mean, sure, people say that to make themselves feel better, but it doesn't change the math. the entropy just keeps increasing. every struggle, every little bit of \"joy\" or \"meaning\" is just localized noise in a system that's fundamentally trending toward nothingness. it feels like we're just trying to decorate a room that's already being demolished. why keep trying to build things up if the end state is always zero? it feels more like we're just wasting resources for no reason.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
